# DSPM (Cyera-like) build rule

12 modules: audit, discovery, classification, risk, access, exposure, encryption_check, shadow, custom_types, compliance, ai_security, remediation. Loop lives in `dspm/loop/` (Discover → Evaluate → Integrate → Validate → Compound).

## Hard rules

1. No paid services, no GPU, no Ollama. Hugging Face `dslim/bert-base-NER` is the only local NER (optional, CPU).
2. Gemini Flash handles 95% of LLM calls. Do not route classification through Sonnet/Opus.
3. Trivy must be 0.70+ / pin 0.71.2. Refuse 0.69.4/0.69.5/0.69.6 (CVE-2026-33634). SHA-pin GitHub Actions; never `trivy-action` mutable tags.
4. Steampipe is a CLI subprocess only (AGPL-3.0). Never `import steampipe`.
5. Presidio installs from `data-privacy-stack/presidio`, not `microsoft/presidio`.
6. Do not auto-approve human PRs. Do not auto-merge `dspm/remediation/policies/`.
7. Dedupe Discover items by SHA-256 of the canonical URL.
8. Keepalive is an in-repo weekly timestamp (`state/keepalive.txt`). Do not use `gautamkrishnar/keepalive-workflow` (repo disabled).
9. Continuous improvement: `dspm loop improve` must consult `catalog.yaml` (forums + GitHub tools + other tools + Python libs), GitHub search, and PyPI — not RSS alone. Next integrations are the gap-audit output. Commercial Purview/Wiz/Prisma are skip.

## CLI

JSON default, `--human` for a table. `make dspm-all` runs every module against `examples/`.
